.TH QFW-STATUS 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Commands"
.SH NAME
qfw-status \- inspect a prepared QFw application runtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qfw-status
.RI [ --run-dir " directory" ]
.RI [ --json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-status
reads the application runtime created by
.BR qfw-setup (1)
and reports its setup state, allocation, directory connection, and recorded
service managers. Application-owned manager health is obtained through the
same service-plane status contract used by the role commands.
.PP
Without
.BR --run-dir ,
the command uses
.B QFW_RUN_TMP_PATH
when set, otherwise the current-run marker below
.BR QFW_RUN_BASE_DIR .
The command does not start, stop, or adopt services.
.PP
The current marker identifies the most recently prepared runtime below one run
base. Launchers managing concurrent runtimes pass
.B --run-dir
explicitly.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --run-dir " directory"
Inspect an explicit application run directory.
.TP
.B --json
Print the complete
.B qfw-runtime-status-v1
JSON object, including the recorded runtime state and manager status objects.
.SH STATES
.TP
.B ready
Setup completed and every recorded application-owned manager is ready.
.TP
.B degraded
Setup completed but a recorded manager is stopped, degraded, or unavailable.
.TP
.B incomplete
The runtime has not completed setup.
.TP
.B failed
Setup recorded an error.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates
.BR ready .
All other runtime states and state-reading errors return nonzero.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-setup (1),
.BR qfw-srun (1),
.BR qfw-teardown (1),
.BR qfw-dir-svc (1),
.BR qfw-qpm-svc (1),
.BR qfw (7)
